THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
================================================================================

This file used to say that third-party licences were "declared in the Maven POM
of the module that depends on it". That is a pointer, not a notice, and it does
not travel with the artifact. It matters here because `dvara-gateway-server`
publishes a repackaged jar with the `app` classifier that physically contains
every runtime dependency named below.

A licence audit of the 121 distinct compile- and runtime-scope dependencies found
no artifact that cannot be redistributed in an Apache-2.0 product, and no
artifact without a declared licence. The obligations that do apply are set out
here.

